<title>ESTONIA: HOTEL OLUMPIA SIGNS SYNDICATED LOAN.</title>
<headline>HOTEL OLUMPIA SIGNS SYNDICATED LOAN.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hotel Olumpia signed a five-year syndicated loan agreement on Wednesday worth 10 million marks, Hansapank said.</p>
<p>The loan interest rate is mark LIBOR plus a margin of 3.75 perent, the bank's interest rate products and financial risks head, Erkki Raasuke, told Reuters.</p>
<p>Raasuke said the loan was organised by Hansapank with Hansabank-Latvija, the Latvian Investment Bank and Forekspank participating.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
